---
/** Slide 03 · The two effects — reduce overwhelm AND enable the impossible. */
---

<section data-slot="03" data-variant="awm-p1" class="deck-section">
  <span class="deck-kicker">03 / 09</span>

  <div>
    <p class="deck-eyebrow mb-3">The thesis</p>
    <h2 class="deck-h2">
      Agents don't just make current work faster. They make
      <span class="deck-gradient">impossible-at-our-size work possible.</span>
    </h2>
  </div>

  <div class="deck-grid mt-2" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));">
    <div class="deck-card flex flex-col gap-2">
      <span class="deck-chip">EFFECT ONE · RELIEF</span>
      <p style="color: var(--color-text-muted); font-size: clamp(1.02rem, 1.15vw, 1.25rem); line-height: 1.55; margin: 0;">
        Reduce overwhelm on work we already do — research, drafts, prep,
        follow-ups.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="deck-card flex flex-col gap-2">
      <span class="deck-chip">EFFECT TWO · EXPANSION</span>
      <p style="color: var(--color-text-muted); font-size: clamp(1.02rem, 1.15vw, 1.25rem); line-height: 1.55; margin: 0;">
        Enable what we currently triage away — ten outreach threads at once,
        conference outreach nine months early, a grant corpus that drafts new
        applications on demand.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="deck-lede mt-2" style="max-width: 64ch;">
    The win is not "same work, faster." It's "stop triaging away the
    high-leverage work."
  </p>
</section>
